            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "#### Let's try a quick problem:",
            "start": 2848,
            "end": 2879
          },
          {
            "id": "p44",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "**Question:** You have **24 grams of Carbon**. How many moles do you have?",
            "start": 2880,
            "end": 2954
          },
          {
            "id": "p45",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "1. **Find Molar Mass:** Look at the periodic table for Carbon $\\rightarrow$ **12 g/mol**.",
            "start": 2956,
            "end": 3045
          },
          {
            "id": "p46",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "2. **Do the math:** ",
            "start": 3046,
            "end": 3066
          },
          {
            "id": "p47",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "equation"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "   $$\\text{Moles} = \\frac{24\\text{ g}}{12\\text{ g/mol}} = \\mathbf{2\\text{ moles}}$$",
            "start": 3067,
            "end": 3150
          },
          {
            "id": "p48",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "That's it! If you have 2 moles of carbon, you also know you have twice Avogadro's number of atoms ($2 \\times 6.022 \\times 10^{23}$).",
            "start": 3152,
            "end": 3284
          },
