            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "1. **A mole is a number:** $6.022 \\times 10^{23}$. Think of it as the \"chemist's dozen.\"",
            "start": 3314,
            "end": 3402
          },
          {
            "id": "p52",
            "category": "STUDY_SUPPORT",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "recap"
            },
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "2. **It connects counting to weighing:** It allows us to count atoms by simply placing them on a scale.",
            "start": 3403,
            "end": 3506
          },
          {
            "id": "p53",
            "category": "STUDY_SUPPORT",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "recap"
            },
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "3. **The Periodic Table is your cheat sheet:** The decimal number under each element tells you how many grams are in 1 mole of that element.",
